DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ddaaeemmoonn() function is for programs wishing to detach themselves from
       the controlling terminal and run in the background as system daemons.

       If  _n_o_c_h_d_i_r is zero, ddaaeemmoonn() changes the process’s current working di‐
       rectory to the root directory ("/"); otherwise, the current working di‐
       rectory is left unchanged.

       If _n_o_c_l_o_s_e is zero, ddaaeemmoonn() redirects standard input, standard output,
       and standard error to _/_d_e_v_/_n_u_l_l; otherwise,  no  changes  are  made  to
       these file descriptors.

